;Match details

* '''Match 1: Leoni def. Morita.''' The champion's first G1 match. Morita — the lowest seed in Block A — fought with Seigigun heart, but the gap in class was clear. Leoni controlled with power: Samoan drop, running hip attack, drive-by. Morita kicked out of the Samoan drop at 2.3 and fought back with a dragon screw and a cross armbreaker attempt, but Leoni powered out and hit the Spear of Fangatapu clean at 15:42. A statement win for the champion. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR POP for Leoni's entrance — the taualga and the namo in the G1 for the first time. '''LEONI''' chants. Respectful applause for Morita. BIG POP for the Spear.

* '''Match 2: Vance def. Marauder.''' The workhorse vs. the mystery. Vance walked to the ring without music — the silence continues. The Marauder's power game was neutralized from the start: Vance used the blueprint Ishida had shown at Episode 10 — mat work, leg attacks, ring awareness. The Marauder grew frustrated. He couldn't find his openings. At 12 minutes, the Marauder went for a power bomb — Vance countered into a DDT. At 14 minutes, Vance hit the half nelson suplex, then the Drill Driver. 1-2-3 at 14:18. The Marauder is 0-1 and exposed. Vance is 1-0 and has not spoken a word since August 5. '''Crowd:''' BUILD for Vance's silent entrance. '''VANCE''' chants. '''SPEAK''' chants during the match. GASPS when Vance countered the power bomb. MEGA POP for the Drill Driver. Standing ovation after — the crowd appreciating the work. Vance did not acknowledge the ovation. He walked to the back.

* '''Match 3: Kengo def. Maeda.''' Kengo's first G1 match alone. No music. No Cannon Club. Maeda — the Kuroshio brother — fought with speed and heart, but Kengo fought with desperation. Eye rake at 3 minutes. Rope grab at 6 minutes. Tights pull at 9 minutes. The finish: Kengo hit a low blow behind the referee's back, then rolled Maeda into a small package. 1-2-3 at 12:33. The crowd booed. Kengo walked out without celebrating. He is 1-0, but the victory told the crowd everything: Kengo cannot win clean. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR HEAT for Kengo's entrance. '''KENGO SUCKS''' chants. '''MAEDA''' chants during the comeback. BOOS for the low blow. BOOS for the finish. Silence as Kengo walked out.

* '''Match 4: Kawada def. Nakamura.''' Two veterans. Strong style vs. unorthodox. The match of the night. 18 minutes of stiff forearms, suplex variations, and fighting spirit. Nakamura kicked out of Kawada's brainbuster at 2.7 — the first time anyone had kicked out of the move in a G1 match. Kawada kicked out of Nakamura's Boma Ye at 2.8. The finish: Kawada hit a second brainbuster — this time from the top rope — at 18:27. Nakamura kicked out at 2.99. The crowd erupted. Kawada did not celebrate. He looked at Nakamura, nodded, and walked to the back. Both men proved they belong in the G1. '''Crowd:''' BUILD for both entrances. '''KAWADA''' and '''NAKAMURA''' dueling chants. '''THIS IS WRESTLING''' during the strike exchanges. GASPS when Nakamura kicked out of the brainbuster. GASPS when Kawada kicked out of the Boma Ye. ERUPTION for the top-rope brainbuster. Standing ovation. '''THIS IS WRESTLING''' chants after.

* '''Match 5: Stan def. Honda.''' The giant vs. the AOPW representative. Stan overpowered Honda from the opening bell — press slam, corner splash, running hip attack. Honda fought back with Asikyran grappling — a takedown, a kneebar attempt, a gutwrench suplex — but Stan's size and power were too much. The chokeslam at 10:15 ended it. Honda kicked out at 2.5, showing the heart that had made him AOPW's choice for the G1, but Stan hit a second chokeslam — this time from the second rope — for the clean pin. Stan is 1-0 and looking dominant. Honda is 0-1 but proved he can hang with the giant. '''Crowd:''' MIXED for Stan's entrance. Respectful POP for Honda. GASPS for Stan's power spots. POP for the chokeslam. Respectful applause for Honda after.

