== Storyline notes ==

* '''The champion's statement.''' Leoni's win over Morita was clean, emphatic, and efficient — the champion enters the G1 as the man to beat. His Round 2 match against Honda in Tokuyama, however, looms: the AOPW representative showed his heart on opening night, kicking out of Big Stan's chokeslam at 2.5 before the second-rope chokeslam ended it.
* '''The blueprint works.''' Vance's dismantling of the Marauder confirmed what Ishida's Episode 10 performance suggested: the undefeated mystery can be outwrestled. The Marauder's power game has no answer for technical wrestling. His Round 2 opponent is Kengo — a man who cannot win clean.
* '''Kengo's mode.''' The low blow + small package finish against Maeda established the terms of Kengo's tournament: he wins with shortcuts or not at all. The crowd's silence as he walked out was the loudest statement of the night.
* '''The veterans deliver.''' Kawada vs. Nakamura was the match of the night and an early tournament-wide match-of-the-tournament candidate. Kawada is 1-0 and Nakamura 0-1, but Nakamura's kickout at 2.99 of the top-rope brainbuster made clear that the loss cost him nothing in standing.
* '''Stan's scale.''' The second-rope chokeslam on Honda was the most visually dominant move of the night. Stan is 1-0 and faces Vance in Round 2 in Tokuyama — the workhorse vs. the giant, with the winner taking early control of Block A.

